17. Revision History

* Version 1.0.0, effective 2026-06-03, was the initial
  independent viewing-only license for the Original Materials.

* Version 1.0.1, effective 2026-06-04, clarified that
  third-party legal material is organized under third-party/
  and that local application-managed runtime data and application
  output remain outside Original Materials except where they
  include protected repository content.

* Version 1.0.2, effective 2026-06-10, strengthened viewing
  limitations, ordinary application use limitations, prohibited
  conduct, artificial-intelligence and dataset restrictions,
  bundled resource and distribution treatment, provenance-sensitive
  material treatment, controlling-text rules, termination
  consequences, severability, and non-waiver provisions.

* Version 1.0.3, effective 2026-06-10, added Japanese governing
  law, Tokyo District Court exclusive first-instance forum
  language, and hosting-service terms clarification.

* Version 1.0.4, effective 2026-06-11, recast the License in a
  more formal rights-reservation structure and clarified the
  distinction between viewing, ordinary application use,
  User Materials, Application Output, Original Materials,
  Third-Party Materials, Distribution Materials, and
  hosting-service functionality.

* Version 1.0.5, effective 2026-06-13, recorded consolidated
  third-party attribution handling and separated third-party
  license texts from the license governing the Original
  Materials.

* Version 2.0.0, effective 2026-06-13, reorganized the License
  around formal definitions of License, Licensor, Licensee,
  Legal Entity, Source Form, Object Form, Work, Derivative Work,
  Original Materials, Repository Contents, Third-Party Materials,
  Provenance-Sensitive Materials, User Materials, Application
  Output, Contribution, Distribution Materials, Ordinary
  Application Use, and AI Use.

* Version 2.1.0, effective 2026-06-13, consolidates the grant
  into one limited-grant section, reduces repeated prohibitory
  wording by relying on defined terms, removes references to an
  unnecessary auxiliary root document, and keeps README as the
  only explanatory repository document that shares the definitions
  stated in this License.
